{"Title":"An Act relative to amateur radio operator license plates","BillNumber":"H3442","DocketNumber":"HD437","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"WMS1","Name":"William M. Straus","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WMS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T17:23:40.337"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"WMS1","Name":"William M. Straus","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/WMS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T17:23:40.3366667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3442/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Straus of Mattapoisett, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3442) of William M. Straus that the Registrar of Motor Vehicles be authorized to issue amateur radio operator license plates.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.  Clause (2) of section 33 of chapter 90 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2016 Official Edition, is hereby amended:\r\n\tby striking, in lines 11-12, the words “; provided, however, the registrar shall collect a similar fee for the issuance of a number plate bearing the station call letters of an amateur radio operator”; and\r\n\tby inserting at the end thereof the following:-\r\n\tNotwithstanding any general or special law, rule, or regulation to the contrary, number plates bearing the station call letters of an amateur radio operator shall be issued without additional charge, and registrations for motor vehicles bearing such plates shall be renewed every two years.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}